When a kconfig repository is declared by an external dependency, use kconfig.overrides to overlay your own .config without modifying the external module. If the source repository was itself created with a .config, the overrides are stacked on top of those base values. The tree is parsed again as the source repository parsed it, from what its manifest records: the variables, the kconfig_version, the write_invisible, and what the tree's $(shell,...) commands answered, so that the overrides are that configuration with other values, not another host's probes: kconfig = use_extension("@rules_kconfig//kconfig:extensions.bzl", "kconfig")
kconfig.overrides( name = "my_board_config", kconfig = "@ext_kconfig//:ext_kconfig", config = "//:.config",
)
use_repo(kconfig, "my_board_config") Then wrap targets that depend on kconfig flags with the generated transition rule: load("@my_board_config//:defs.bzl", "with_kconfig_overrides") with_kconfig_overrides( name = "ext_config_customized", actual = "@ext_kconfig//:config",
) Values explicitly set on the command line take precedence over the overlay.

