load("@rules_kconfig//kconfig:defs.bzl", "make_variable_setting") make_variable_setting(name, equals, expression, type) A build setting whose value is a toolchain's "Make" variable, for settings_labels. The variables come from the targets of the common toolchains attribute, which provide TemplateVariableInfo: Bazel's C++ toolchain (@bazel_tools//tools/cpp:current_cc_toolchain) has CC, C_COMPILER, LD, NM, OBJCOPY, STRIP and more, rules_rust's (@rules_rust//rust/toolchain:current_rust_toolchain) has RUSTC, RUSTDOC and CARGO. The value is a string as expanded, an int, or a bool that says whether the expansion equals a text: make_variable_setting( name = "cc", expression = "$(CC)", toolchains = ["@bazel_tools//tools/cpp:current_cc_toolchain"],
) make_variable_setting( name = "cc_is_clang", equals = "clang", expression = "$(C_COMPILER)", toolchains = ["@bazel_tools//tools/cpp:current_cc_toolchain"], type = "bool",
) Named in settings_labels, such a target gives a CONFIG_* symbol the value of the toolchain Bazel resolved for the build, in config.h and the transitions, where the repository rule saw only the variables of env. A value that takes running the compiler (a $(cc-option,...) probe) is not a Make variable; see the documentation on env for those. ATTRIBUTES Name Description Type Mandatory Default name A unique name for this target. Name required equals For type = "bool": the setting is true when the expansion is this text. String optional "" expression The text to expand, with $(NAME) references to Make variables. String required type The type of the setting: string, int or bool. String optional "string"
